The two dominant EJR constraints remain unchanged: the size-6 3-cohesive bloc on {x1,x2,x3} forces |W ∩ {x1,x2,x3}| ≥ 2 (otherwise no member of the bloc reaches ℓ=3), while the size-4 2-cohesive bloc on {y4,y5,y6} forces at least two seats from {y4,y5,y6,z1,z2}. The latter two seats lie outside A1, immediately capping |W ∩ A1| ≤ 3; the former already guarantees |W ∩ A1| ≥ 2.  

