The 6-voter 3-cohesive x-group forces at least two x-candidates into any valid W (otherwise no member reaches ℓ=3 even with private candidates), immediately giving voter 1 a lower bound of 2. The 4-voter 2-cohesive y-group symmetrically requires two seats from {y4,y5,y6,z1,z2}, all outside A1, so the intersection cannot exceed 3. The two explicit EJR committees {x1,x2,y4,y5,z1} and {x1,x2,x3,y4,y5} realize exactly these values.

