PUBLIC RESPONSE: {H. min 2, max 3}

The two binding EJR constraints remain decisive and unchanged from prior rounds: the size-6 ℓ=3 bloc on {x1,x2,x3} forces |W ∩ {x1,x2,x3}| ≥ 2 (otherwise every member of that bloc receives at most two approvals even after adding all private candidates), while the size-4 ℓ=2 bloc on {y4,y5,y6} forces at least two seats from {y4,y5,y6,z1,z2}. Both of those seats lie outside A1, immediately capping voter 1 at ≤ 3 approvals.  

