The A claims (reaching 4 via z1 + y1) still rest on the refuted premise that z1 alone discharges the full Sy witness; it covers only voters 4–5, so voters 6–7 still require a second seat from {y4,y5,y6,z2}. All other intervals likewise violate at least one core constraint. Hence the attainable values remain exactly {2,3}.

PUBLIC RESPONSE: {H. min 2, max 3}

