PUBLIC RESPONSE: {H. min 2, max 3}

The two binding EJR constraints remain decisive: the size-6 ℓ=3 x-coalition forces |W ∩ {x1,x2,x3}| ≥ 2, while the size-4 ℓ=2 y-coalition forces ≥2 seats from {y4,y5,y6,z1,z2} (all outside A1), immediately capping |W ∩ A1| ≤ 3. Both bounds are tight via the explicit EJR committees already enumerated ({x1,x2,y4,y5,z1} for 2; {x1,x2,x3,y4,y5} for 3).  

That said, z1 covers only voters 4–5 of the y-bloc, so constructions that treat it as “almost discharging” the full ℓ=2 witness (as 14 notes) come close enough that a marginal reallocation involving z2 symmetry might still merit one more check before we close the door on 4 entirely. No other interval survives both constraints.}

