The two A holdouts rest on the refuted premise that z1 alone can discharge the full Sy witness. It covers only voters 4–5; voters 6–7 still require a second dedicated seat from {y4,y5,y6,z2}, restoring the two-seat requirement outside A1. Any attempt to insert y1/z3 (e.g., {x1,x2,y1,y4,z1}) therefore leaves voters 6–7 with only one approved winner, violating EJR for Sy. No other interval survives both constraints simultaneously.

